TITLE: 2. M2 native C++20 engine replacing Xyce on core analog

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLAN-V2-005
STATUS: InProgress
TITLE: M2a - C++20 linear core, SuiteSparse KLU and in-process NativeCppBackend
STATEMENT: >>>
Implement CSC sparse assembly with pre-bound device slots, SuiteSparse KLU shared-library adapter (real/complex, symbolic reuse), dense reference solver, linear primitives (R/C/L/K/V/I waveforms/E/F/G/H), OP/DC/AC/TRAN drivers, full spice_capi.h execution API, and in-process NativeCppBackend via LibraryImport/SafeHandle.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Phase: M2
Depends-on: PLAN-V2-001, PLAN-V2-002
Deliverables: cpp/linalg (SparseLu + DenseLu + KLU adapter), cpp/devices (R/C/L/K/V/I/E/F/G/H + waveforms), cpp/analysis (OP/DC sweep/AC/TRAN BE/Trap/BDF2 + UIC + breakpoints), cpp/audit (DC/AC/TRAN physical audits), include/spice/capi.h & cpp/capi/capi.cpp (ABI v2.1: SPICE deck parser, Diode, DC sweep, NOISE, HB, PSS, SP, BDF2, complex result introspection), NativeCppBackend in Spice.Sdk (DllImportResolver for SPICE_V2_CAPI_LIB + RunSpiceDeckAsync + full ABI v2.1 contiguous buffer marshaling).
Verification: GCC 12 and Clang 14 C++20 -Werror builds pass all 8 CTest binaries (41 C++20 tests, 0.11 s; GCC gcov -b 80.23% lines / 46.23% branches across 18 owned .cpp files) AND .NET 11.0.100 NativeCppBackend passes 14/14 live xUnit tests + Spice.App smoke tests against libspice_capi.so. Remaining to close M2a: vcpkg SuiteSparse KLU link test and head-to-head XyceBackend/ngspice SANDLER8/SANDLER9 comparison.
<<<
